math-academy-id "q-282146" :question/problem "Let $a=2i-7j+4k$ and $b=5i+3j-6k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,+\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-7)(-6)-(4)(3))i-((2)(-6)-(4)(5))j+((2)(3)-(-7)(5))k \\\\  & =(42-12)i-(-12-20)j+(6+35)k \\\\  & =30\\,i+32\\,j+41\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-282146/field-1" "q-282146/field-2" "q-282146/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282146"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103542/selection/3ac783692e310bc42d0f1aad80c6084a00382a61423de2566e3d9b4b255e4c2a" :answer/id #uuid "cca606c9-e50d-5425-957b-db71a8fabb2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3,9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103542/selection/faf2b46de244a884108810a181c63e7c489c91e9e930fa6465674ca44d779944" :answer/id #uuid "060ebcab-6b34-56bb-8d67-1f0732937168" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103542/selection/5dd40cb23e1e39b1a29875443780a68c8e4b95acd07d2fb088b222cf6cc96dcc" :answer/id #uuid "67bd8ad0-1d67-5cfc-9ba2-2a3490c2a63a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3},3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103542/selection/7f44eea92af5c9acdec8919ce008f32aaa724d76d416ab5243173911577f9642" :answer/id #uuid "dbca431f-f8c5-5370-8367-5080f10591bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103542/selection/73626b9872a8e0d9a206aee09c0a6f81b943d849a126e247740edbf6c67b430a" :answer/id #uuid "5b9b933a-4328-5b02-9c83-1bc0b01b08dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103542/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ffd1811-7344-5aa4-a404-ef0f34a29eb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103542/selection/7f44eea92af5c9acdec8919ce008f32aaa724d76d416ab5243173911577f9642" :answer-field/choices ["q-103542/selection/3ac783692e310bc42d0f1aad80c6084a00382a61423de2566e3d9b4b255e4c2a" "q-103542/selection/faf2b46de244a884108810a181c63e7c489c91e9e930fa6465674ca44d779944" "q-103542/selection/5dd40cb23e1e39b1a29875443780a68c8e4b95acd07d2fb088b222cf6cc96dcc" "q-103542/selection/7f44eea92af5c9acdec8919ce008f32aaa724d76d416ab5243173911577f9642" "q-103542/selection/73626b9872a8e0d9a206aee09c0a6f81b943d849a126e247740edbf6c67b430a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103542" :question/id #uuid "fa58a80f-ad5f-57b3-8136-8bf6f43c733c" :question/math-academy-id "q-103542" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,2x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-x,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{355}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 2x & 3 \\\\ 2 & -x & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2x \\\\ 2 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2x+3x)i-(-1-6)j+(x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨5x,7,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}+49+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ \\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49} & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ 34{x}^{2}+49 & =355 \\\\ 34{x}^{2} & =306 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103542/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103542"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-282269/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "7220f6dc-804a-5952-8aa2-ece7984a6d00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282269/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "05874c5d-4db0-5490-990d-5497c811900e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282269/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d308653-8f1e-5f72-8077-913f2fa9da55" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282269/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-282269/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-282269/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282269" :question/id #uuid "e1f66b62-a151-5b00-bab4-0cd70c1a41f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-282269" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{10}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(3x-1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨3,1-3x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(1-3x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-6x+11} & =\\sqrt{10} \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-6x+11 & =10 \\\\ (3x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-282269/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282269"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-282262/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "c5155a28-22dd-54d9-904d-52eb3db422cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282262/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "50096657-96ad-5bc8-923d-da3a399564ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282262/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-282262/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282262/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "8c56013b-cca9-556f-bfe4-7260efbe46bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282262/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e24a0b4-61de-584c-94ac-928507f054ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282262/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-282262/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282262" :question/id #uuid "a06a34cd-d85e-589e-9964-4d0cd1f43e22" :question/math-academy-id "q-282262" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,3,0⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{49}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 0 \\\\ -x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(x+0)j+(0+3x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-x,3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+9 & =49 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2,$ $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-282262/field-1" "q-282262/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282262"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103540/selection/592b9f18cf04a8c75d513e20b1b4a536540e9c3c0f5c7614ffaf1943dc6c7d15" :answer/id #uuid "f55e0fa3-387c-5657-a2fc-ea0bceb8031f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103540/selection/3ce4df282068008b57541e2a0e43bc84a3288a422ec13a7d88100704c030c662" :answer/id #uuid "1b4ec3dd-346e-55d6-baa9-200d86a229b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103540/selection/2d72fb9577d14e692ee0c494e42dfc349f511e1def3de9a4ad7e2ebebd23a09a" :answer/id #uuid "faedcfc3-3fa8-5c20-bf7a-c72cd7261dee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103540/selection/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee" :answer/id #uuid "db20040e-bef4-51cd-947b-ee90d170929d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103540/selection/7ce38f588ba6fc884b759194aacd3912390f21a141062a40e7d3a3db5b001295" :answer/id #uuid "6daa0145-bf33-529f-bb3b-02149dfe6f9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-4,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103540/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eab3d72b-5fd5-575e-b41f-09cd5ece7d50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103540/selection/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee" :answer-field/choices ["q-103540/selection/592b9f18cf04a8c75d513e20b1b4a536540e9c3c0f5c7614ffaf1943dc6c7d15" "q-103540/selection/3ce4df282068008b57541e2a0e43bc84a3288a422ec13a7d88100704c030c662" "q-103540/selection/2d72fb9577d14e692ee0c494e42dfc349f511e1def3de9a4ad7e2ebebd23a09a" "q-103540/selection/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee" "q-103540/selection/7ce38f588ba6fc884b759194aacd3912390f21a141062a40e7d3a3db5b001295"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103540" :question/id #uuid "f571d284-38ad-50ae-b89e-87bf4db6e4ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-103540" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨x,1,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{93}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 2 \\\\ x & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 2 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ x & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3-2)i-(-2x-2x)j+(2x-3x)k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25} & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+25 & =93 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =68 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-103540/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103540"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-282260/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "4d3c239f-a333-5d88-ae92-08380d731a45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282260/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5e8eaf8-51e0-5844-8acf-f4e6db888966" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282260/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-282260/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282260/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c4dcc068-e785-52f8-bc25-d5e3ae981a4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282260/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "330de255-3b94-5b56-9e5a-f8f0c53758db" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282260/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-282260/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282260" :question/id #uuid "1dba81c8-6f48-528d-b583-abc4c231bef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-282260" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2x,0,4⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{280}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 1 \\\\ -2x & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ -2x & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -2x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(12-0)i-(8x+2x)j+(0+6x)k \\\\  & =⟨12,-10x,6x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{12}^{2}+(-10x)^{2}+(6x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+100{x}^{2}+36{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ \\sqrt{136{x}^{2}+144} & =\\sqrt{280} \\\\ 136{x}^{2}+144 & =280 \\\\ 136{x}^{2} & =136 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-1,$ $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-282260/field-1" "q-282260/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282260"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4341"] :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4343"] :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
